<!--
  reloy.ir sitemap.

  Only pages that serve real content to a signed-out stranger are listed. The
  app shells (/signin, /owner, /staff) and the API are deliberately absent and
  are also disallowed in robots.txt.

  "/" is NOT listed. The server answers it with the customer wallet shell
  (index.html); the hop to the onboarding site happens in JavaScript
  (index.guard.js), which non-rendering crawlers never run. Listing it would
  invite indexing of an empty wallet. It belongs here once the root serves the
  onboarding page itself.

  Each <url> carries the full set of xhtml:link alternates, itself included —
  that is what the spec requires, and it states the language pairing in a way
  every crawler reads without executing JavaScript.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9"
        xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">

